# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_units_meter.py" "UNITS METER GATE: PASS" "units meter" "units meter v2 (the PURE, content-free billing computation: Units = in-scope LOC × an entanglement premium, run over Veripsa's OWN code graph [build_graph output only — paths/edge-kinds/line-counts, never code bodies; aggregate scalars, never a per-pair list]. premium = min(CAP_PREMIUM, 1 + a_xs·xs_intensity + a_call·min(call_density,CAP) + a_xdir·min(xdir_density,CAP) + a_blast·min(blast_mean,CAP) + a_hub·hub_bucket + a_cc·min(cochange_blind,CAP)). The language-AGNOSTIC cross-substrate term [shared tables/config touched by >=2 files + migration<->query pairs, name-based] is the crown jewel — weighted most and UNCAPPED — while EVERY other term is CAPPED so a namespace language's 10-50x import fan-out / a hot method name cannot run the bill away, and CAP_PREMIUM bounds the TOTAL. Two structural terms: resolved CALLS [the fairer cross-language signal, precision-biased for billing via STOP-list + <=3-def fan-out] AND cross-directory imports. A CO-CHANGE term [git history files-that-change-together with NO code edge, lift-corrected, the 2nd detector] enters as a pure scalar derived offline from git-log filenames-only. LOC is the language-agnostic base. Coefficients PROVISIONAL/owner-tunable in one labeled _UNIT_POLICY dict [PO: not finalized]. Asserts: units>0 & premium>=1.0 & v2 component shape; SPLIT-INVARIANCE [same code split across two files does NOT inflate units — LOC-anchored, within ~10%]; coupled repo earns a HIGHER premium than a flat one; import caps BOUND a pathological fan-out; the CALL term lifts premium [and a STOP-listed name does NOT bill]; the CO-CHANGE term lifts premium and is cap-bounded [raw density stored]; CAP_PREMIUM clamps a runaway xs premium [flagged premium_capped]; the offline git co-change path runs end-to-end on a real repo. No Postgres — fully offline)" "units meter v2 (pure content-free billing: in-scope LOC × capped entanglement premium over the code graph + offline git co-change; split-invariant, coupling-sensitive, calls+imports+xs+co-change all bounded under a global premium cap; provisional owner-tunable coefficients; no DB)" 10
